From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: a flashing window's taskbar button turns orange; the shell hands the foreground to its own programs

The taskbar is a shell hook window: HSHELL_FLASH turns the window's button
orange (three blinks, then lit until the window is activated or stops
flashing), as Windows' taskbar does for a window the foreground lock kept
back. The shell's pieces run in programs of their own (sg-shell's Start,
Magnifier, the notification centre, Settings): asked to show themselves on
the person's key or click, they get the right to come forward
(AllowSetForegroundWindow, as Windows' shell grants its hosts). Win+D gives
the keyboard to the desktop's icons, not the taskbar.
---
 programs/explorer/explorer_private.h |  6 +++
 programs/explorer/shellkeys.c        | 22 +++++++++
 programs/explorer/systray.c          | 96 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 124 insertions(+)

--- a/programs/explorer/explorer_private.h
+++ b/programs/explorer/explorer_private.h
